1
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:32,960
Thank you.

2
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:33,177
My heart was all aflutter
when I found out Davis'

3
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:37,157
soccer team was playing against that
dreamy superstar Ken with Rocket.

4
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:41,177
Davis started off great, but when Ken got
in the game, he ran circles around him.

5
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:44,537
Afterwards, Cody discovered another
control spire in the Digi-World,

6
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:46,257
but the ground swallowed us up.

7
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:48,537
The Emperor made Davis
choose which one of us would

8
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:51,157
be We fed to the Deltamon
when suddenly we showed up,

9
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:54,437
and Davis realized it was
just the Emperor's sick joke.

10
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:58,860
We found out that my dreamboat
Ken is really the Digimon Emperor!

11
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:13,540
I could and I am Ken Ichijoji!

12
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:15,960
I'm dreaming!

13
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,060
Ken is the Digimon Emperor?

14
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:22,377
The one and only, well, Davis,
farewell for now, my worthy adversary,

15
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:24,225
until we meet again in battle.

16
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:33,189
Uh-oh, the Emperor's not in a good mood
today, which is like every other day.

17
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:35,051
Maybe I can cheer him up.

18
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,395
Hey, Ken, did you hear the
one about the man who was...

19
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,659
I guess you heard that one already.

20
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:44,745
Master, what are you watching?

21
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:48,960
Join us as we talk with
young genius Ken Itchy Joji.

22
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:51,940
I'm just your average boy, genius.

23
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:53,260
You're so modest.

24
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,897
Do you spend a lot of time studying?

25
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:57,627
Some geniuses do, but
I'd rather play soccer.

26
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,940
And funny, too.

27
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:02,520
They say genius is 1 %
brains and 99 % hard work.

28
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,137
Do you think that's true?

29
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:05,317
Mine's 2%.

30
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,660
You are funny.

31
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:10,657
And to think you came from such humble
beginnings in an everyday apartment building.

32
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:12,577
Are you glad you're just
a normal, average kid?

33
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:16,117
Yeah, there's absolutely nothing
I love more than being average.

34
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:20,860
So, you've mastered chess, 3D chess,
and the Donkey Madness video game.

35
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:23,120
Is there anything you can't handle?

36
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,010
Reporters?

37
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,197
The big question on everyone's
mind is what does a genius

38
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:31,237
do for fun when he's not
solving complex math problems?

39
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:34,857
Though I know that math is already
more fun than most people can handle.

40
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:39,037
Well, I'm always busy writing one of my
computer programs, but like I said earlier,

41
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,897
my favorite thing to do is play soccer.

42
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:43,980
I'm sure you'll be a big
success at that, too, Ken.

43
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:47,494
I don't see how anything could
possibly get in your way.

44
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:52,400
Well, that about wraps it up.

45
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:54,109
Thanks for your time, Ken.

46
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:56,400
Best of luck. You're welcome.

47
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:59,156
That went well, don't you think, Ken?

48
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:00,730
Of course.

49
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,577
I always look good to the press.

50
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:07,297
That 1%, 2 % stuff was brilliant, although
I'm not really sure I understand it.

51
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:08,957
I'll explain it to you later.

52
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,922
There's something else
you can help me with, too.

53
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,877
How do you get past level
four on Donkey Madness?

54
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,666
I just can't get the Scepter.

55
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:22,121
Of course you know I wouldn't tell
anyone else your gaming secrets.

56
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:25,071
I'd be glad to tell you everything I know.

57
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:27,337
I'll even come over and
help you play the game.

58
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:32,017
That is, of course, if you don't think
you're too old to be playing video games.

59
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:33,380
Oh, yeah, too old.

60
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:35,637
I always forget that I'm an adult.

61
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:37,460
Oh, look at the time.

62
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:40,406
I've got to get to my
advanced joystick class.

63
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:43,900
Oh, could you do just one
last thing for me, Ken?

64
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:47,200
What is it? Um, autograph?

65
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:49,930
Hmm.

66
00:04:50,013 --> 00:04:50,860
Here you go.

67
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:52,290
Thanks, Ken.

68
00:04:52,373 --> 00:04:53,320
You are the best.

69
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:56,077
Even better than a
graphics accelerator card.

70
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:57,631
The guys will be jealous.

71
00:04:58,660 --> 00:04:59,490
Fool.

72
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,590
Cheer up.

73
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,720
You can destroy somebody tomorrow.

74
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:09,600
Oh, Ken, honey, your
dinner is ready, dear.

75
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,580
Ken, it's getting cold.

76
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:20,460
It's your favorite, dear, liver
squash and lumpy mashed potatoes.

77
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:23,280
Saw you on the TV today, Tiger.

78
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:26,077
Soon you're gonna need a stick
to keep all of the ladies away,

79
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:27,513
just like your old dad.

80
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:29,380
I've lost my appetite.

81
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:30,830
Oh!

82
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:32,332
Well, what's the matter?

83
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:33,290
Nothing.

84
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:40,337
Look at all of those fools out there
Dreaming away their meaningless lives

85
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:46,380
Running around like rats in a maze Not one
of them is worth half of what I'm worth

86
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,160
Nothing but fools

87
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:57,580
Master? Master? Master?

88
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:03,760
Don't be depressed I've got an idea.

89
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,597
Let's grab some Dark Rings.

90
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:07,497
We'll capture a couple of innocent Digimon

91
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:10,051
and make their lives absolutely miserable.

92
00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:11,968
That should make you happy.

93
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:15,640
You mean Ken is the Digimon Emperor?

94
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:17,250
Right.

95
00:06:17,333 --> 00:06:18,877
And as Emperor, he's not just a genius.

96
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:20,136
He's an evil genius.

97
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:22,280
And a super evil genius at that.

98
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,577
I just don't understand why
such a talented and smart

99
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:28,197
person would want to use
their gifts to hurt others.

100
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,317
He seems so nice.

101
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:32,600
You know, there was a report
on him on TV yesterday.

102
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:35,177
I saw it on that show, The Genius Parade.

103
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:38,378
I can't believe the Digimon
Emperor is a kid like us.

104
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:39,540
Let's find him.

105
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:42,140
What? Find him? Yeah.

106
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:45,997
We'll track him down and confront
him outside the digital world.

107
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:48,917
Does his plan include a
part where we get to eat?

108
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,200
For you, anything.

109
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:52,720
Hey, I wonder where Yo-Li could be.

110
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:55,380
Hey, everybody.

111
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,257
Sorry I'm late, but look what I've got.

112
00:06:57,340 --> 00:06:58,540
Chocolate! Cookies!

113
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:02,517
You're the best, Yoli.

114
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:05,337
You could be head chef
in the cafeteria one day.

115
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:07,460
So, you're not hungry? What?

116
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,925
I'm surprised they didn't
eat my arm right off.

117
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,600
Oh, I found this.

118
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,999
There's an article in it about Ken.

119
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,240
I'll take that.

120
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:25,760
Hey, you gave me a paper cut.

121
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,744
Yeah, that's him, the evil kid.

122
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:35,571
Who would think that such a normal-looking
boy could be the Digimon Emperor?

123
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,960
His smile makes him look so gentle.

124
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:41,917
Oh, yeah, but his haircut
makes him look like you, Kari.

125
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,060
Let me see it.

126
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,600
Oh, this kid.

127
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:48,100
I've seen him on the news before.

128
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:49,580
Look at his IQ.

129
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,097
He could program my computer any day.

130
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,017
Are you crazy?

131
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:56,337
He may be smart, but that guy is
completely rotten to the core.

132
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:57,980
Well, he's not just smart.

133
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:00,180
He's got dash and good looks, too.

134
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:02,680
And he's also really athletic.

135
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:06,360
Hey, I'm just as good at
sports as that guy is.

136
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:10,017
Okay, okay, don't get your
knickers in a twist, Davis.

137
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:11,217
Let's just find him.

138
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:12,359
What are knickers?

139
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:13,440
Never mind.

140
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:16,477
I'll use my math program to locate the

141
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:18,497
apartment building behind
Ken in this picture.

142
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:20,117
Looks like a nice place to live.

143
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:23,717
Yeah, if living next to a heartless kid
who wants to rule the world is nice.

144
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:28,180
If my calculations are correct,
he should live right around here.

145
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:31,500
Yeah, I know that area.

146
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:33,074
You smudged my screen.

147
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:37,237
I think there's an apartment building
right there under Kari's fingerprint.

148
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,150
Can?

149
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,190
Can?

150
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:42,410
What's up?

151
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:47,379
Well, usually I hear the furious
scribble of him doing math problems.

152
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:49,520
But today, nothing.

153
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:52,817
He's been awfully quiet
since that soccer game.

154
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:54,371
I don't want to barge in.

155
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:56,877
I might set off one of his booby traps.

156
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,597
When you met with his teacher,
did he say anything at all to you?

157
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:03,897
No, all his teacher could talk about
was something called donkey madness.

158
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:04,862
Donkey madness?

159
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:06,837
I know, it's strange.

160
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:08,979
I mean, we don't even own a donkey.

161
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:12,239
Let's go in there.

162
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:13,637
Oh, should we do that?

163
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,357
I say we break down the door.

164
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,270
What?

165
00:09:16,353 --> 00:09:17,352
No, don't break it down.

166
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:19,540
Well, I've got to break something.

167
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,030
Hey!

168
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:22,050
Ooh.

169
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,030
Ken?

170
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,520
Look at this!

171
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,500
What's this?

172
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,300
Goodbye to all of you.

173
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:41,777
Your trivial lives will
plague me no longer.

174
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:43,040
My destiny awaits.

175
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,070
No!

176
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,300
He's run away!

177
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,360
Here it is.

178
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:56,138
This is the place where we
stop Ken once and for all.

179
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,541
Okay, I wrote down a battle plan.

180
00:09:58,780 --> 00:10:00,604
Uh, does it include the police?

181
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:02,510
Huh?

182
00:10:02,593 --> 00:10:03,423
Man, that kid's trouble.

183
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:09,629
Little Ken and Chijoji is missing, and
no one has any idea where he might be.

184
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:13,200
I think he's run away from home.

185
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:15,320
Run away from home?

186
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:17,246
I bet I know where he's gone.

187
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:18,760
Speak to me.

188
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:19,690
Just two words.

189
00:10:19,773 --> 00:10:20,603
That's plenty.

190
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,715
I think you're right.

191
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:43,937
Ken is probably in the digital world,
but it's dangerous to just rush in there.

192
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:47,597
But the longer we wait, the more
time he has to plot against us.

193
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:49,268
We need to make a new plan.

194
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:51,701
We need to know what Ken's doing.

195
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:53,611
Let's check the computer.

196
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:56,076
Does that mean what I think it means?

197
00:10:57,660 --> 00:11:01,778
Ken is taking over areas in the
digital world faster than ever before.

198
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,195
Well, then, let's go.

199
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:05,104
We can't afford to be reckless.

200
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:08,657
Remember the expression, fools
rush in where angels fear to tread.

201
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:10,417
So what do you think we should do?

202
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:11,330
You know,

203
00:11:11,413 --> 00:11:13,257
being a fool is really
low on my priority list,

204
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,752
but I can't just sit here and do nothing.

205
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,760
Why do evil geniuses have to be so evil?

206
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:23,172
He doesn't look capable of
causing such trouble, you know?

207
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:26,440
Well, he is, and don't
let yourself forget it.

208
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:30,000
Well, I've had enough talk.

209
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:33,617
The clock keeps ticking away
and I'm getting ticked off.

210
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:34,820
I want some action.

211
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:36,957
He's right, so let's get it into gear.

212
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:38,940
Yeah. I'm with you. Let's fight.

213
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:41,057
You've convinced me.

214
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:42,258
No more hesitation.

215
00:11:43,820 --> 00:11:44,650
Excellent.

216
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:46,140
Digi-port, open.

217
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:49,760
Let's go get that evil cute guy!

218
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,080
It's genius stomping time, let's go!

219
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:07,020
Look at this land of fire!

220
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:10,100
It's like the movie Land of Fire! I know.

221
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:12,480
Sure is hot!

222
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,000
Five star chili hot!

223
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:19,740
Why don't you let me fight Instead
of capturing Greymon You fight?

224
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:25,340
I guess I'll take that as a no

225
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,137
Master, can I get a little help here?

226
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:30,102
I'm having some trouble standing

227
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:32,380
I'm okay

228
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:38,060
That control spire will be their doom

229
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:41,460
Keep your eyes open
Trouble could be anywhere

230
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:48,490
Meramon!

231
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,600
Meramon are very dangerous.

232
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:57,677
They can burn you with their roaring
flame attack or just by touching you.

233
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,360
Let's show them who's boss.

234
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,460
Digi-Armor, energize!

235
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:07,870
Digimon.

236
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:11,180
V-mon, armor, digivolts, dude!

237
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:17,800
Digimon, digital monsters,
Digimon are the champions!

238
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:20,320
Conflamedramon, the fire of courage!

239
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:23,360
Raring flame!

240
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:24,660
Fire rocket!

241
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:31,764
Don't do that anymore,
you're just tickling him!

242
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:35,057
I don't think fire attacks
are going to work on them!

243
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:35,970
My turn!

244
00:13:36,053 --> 00:13:37,680
Get him, Hawkmon!

245
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:43,120
Digi-Armor in our time!

246
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:46,520
Digimon!

247
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:49,560
Hawkmon armor Digiball 2!

248
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:56,840
Digimon, digital monsters,
Digimon are the champions!

249
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:00,360
Pulsemon, the wings of love!

250
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:02,120
Digimon!

251
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,480
Tempest wing!

252
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:14,701
Gazimon, stop!

253
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,782
You're making the flames digger!

254
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:23,180
There's my prey!

255
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:27,620
Come and get it!

256
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:31,657
What do you say the two of us go at it?

257
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:32,657
One-on-one?

258
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:37,480
As much as I appreciate your offer,
Koromon, I'd rather we play Sphere Throw.

259
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:39,550
What?

260
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:42,500
But I hate Sphere Throw.

261
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:44,057
Nothing is working.

262
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:45,905
It's up to you, Armadillo-Mom.

263
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:48,500
Digi-Armor Energize!

264
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,740
Armadillo-Mom, Armor Digivolve to...

265
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:06,040
Digimon, digital monsters,
Digimon are the champions!

266
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:10,360
Digimon, the drill of power! Digimon!

267
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,040
Rock cracking!

268
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,200
Way to go!

269
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:26,780
Look!

270
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,180
Watch out!

271
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:31,699
Nothing stops him!

272
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:35,620
Here they come!

273
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:41,380
Let's do it!

274
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:43,440
Digimon armor energized!

275
00:15:47,740 --> 00:15:49,500
Otomon armor digivolts!

276
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:58,740
Pegasmon flying host on Tempest wing.

277
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:02,700
It's working!

278
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:08,460
Store shower!

279
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:12,080
Are you ready?

280
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:13,280
Always am!

281
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:15,920
Digi Armor, energize!

282
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:19,840
Digimon! Gatrimon!

283
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:22,580
Armor Digivolve, too! Digimon!

284
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:23,642
Digiro Monster!

285
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:25,389
Digimon are the champions!

286
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:35,120
Sending Greymon to attack
those kids is my best plan yet!

287
00:16:35,660 --> 00:16:38,895
But, uh, what about the
problems you had with Andromon?

288
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,897
I learned from my mistakes.

289
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:43,957
If I can make a rookie Digimon
digivolve while under my control,

290
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:46,277
then I can control its
other forms as well!

291
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:48,797
Master, you give me chills
when you act all tough.

292
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:49,710
Oh, be quiet.

293
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,976
Greymon, digivolve to metal,
Greymon, and be my slave!

294
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,060
Greymon Digimon, too!

295
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:06,140
Skull Greymon!

296
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:09,660
Rosetta Stone!

297
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:14,620
That's what you get for playing with fire!

298
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:21,037
Oh, no!

299
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,520
It's Skull Greymon!

300
00:17:23,860 --> 00:17:27,537
The only thing more terrifying than
his looks are his fighting skills,

301
00:17:27,620 --> 00:17:29,520
especially his dark shot attack.

302
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:32,240
Skull? Greymon?

303
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:49,000
Suddenly, this plan doesn't
really seem so good.

304
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:55,680
How can we beat that thing?

305
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:57,440
I have no idea!

306
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,060
Not even one?

307
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,060
I have one!

308
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:03,530
What?

309
00:18:03,613 --> 00:18:06,540
I said we run and then
after that we run some more!

310
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,400
Fire Rocket!

311
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,560
He got Flamedermon!

312
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:23,420
Digmon, no!

313
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:33,770
Possimon!

314
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:37,360
Everyone, run!

315
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:40,020
But we have to fight Skull Greymon!

316
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:41,081
Yes, great idea.

317
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:43,537
Stay clustered together so
you create an easy target.

318
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:44,450
Get to safety!

319
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:47,320
Dark Shot!

320
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,020
He's got good aim.

321
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:03,900
I should probably put on my goggles!

322
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:11,680
You wanna play rough?

323
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:15,833
I'm afraid to find out who he's calling.

324
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:20,980
What are those things?

325
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,886
Look, they're Dark Tyranomon!

326
00:19:27,060 --> 00:19:31,460
A computer program turned Tyranomon
into the evil Dark Tyranomon!

327
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:33,856
Watch out for his fire breath attack!

328
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:36,540
Why can't we ever fight anything short?

329
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,440
Like some mice!

330
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:40,610
Yeah!

331
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:42,160
It's going way too far!

332
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:45,077
With all that fire, they can
bake, broil and freeze him!

333
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:48,017
If he can't stand the heat, he
better get out of the kitchen!

334
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:50,335
Stop, you're making me wanna barbecue!

335
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:59,771
He's throwing them around like drag dolls!

336
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:01,770
Painful!

337
00:20:01,853 --> 00:20:04,664
Hope he doesn't get the
idea to throw us around.

338
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:10,682
He beats them all single-handed!

339
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:18,140
That's Agumon!

340
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:20,777
That slimy creature is coming after him!

341
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:23,331
And when I say slimy creature, I mean Ken.

342
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:25,460
Agumon! Let him go!

343
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,130
Agumon!

344
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:29,460
You better not hurt him, Ken!

345
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:30,660
Dad, jerk!

346
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:33,275
From defeat, I snatch another victory!

347
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:36,050
T .K.

348
00:20:36,260 --> 00:20:38,040
Davis, somebody do something!

349
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,435
They're getting away!

350
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:45,130
Whoa,

351
00:20:45,213 --> 00:20:49,747
that's the strangest thing I've seen
since my ethernet configuration collapsed.

352
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:51,850
What?

353
00:20:51,933 --> 00:20:56,537
The entire area that Agumon was guarding
has been taken over by the Digimon Emperor!

354
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:59,444
Does that mean that Agumon
is under his control?

355
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:02,586
Or worse yet, what if
Agumon's been destroyed?

356
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:04,180
Then who's next?

357
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:09,106
If he was able to get Agumon, that means
every one of our Digimon are in danger!

358
